To consolidate retrieval, the system unions the top-100 candidates from each pool. A LightGBM [ke2017lightgbm] ranker then scores and calibrates this final list. Table tab:features outlines the input feature schema. The model ingests individual ranks and scores from both pools, alongside their cross-pool RRF metrics. Turn number, request category, and goal specificity define the session context. Non-retrieved candidates receive sentinel values. Training uses out-of-fold scoring to prevent data leakage from the 8B retrieval model.

